% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Analysis and reduced form
%
% Every layer is cut into elementary layers with one generator each.  The
% input discs cut the tangle into connectors (pieces made of cups, caps and
% straight strands), which are planar matchings between the strands above
% and below.  Closed loops inside a connector bound empty discs.  Two
% neighbouring strands that pass a disc on the same side and are joined by a
% cup or a cap right before or after it form a finger, which is pulled back
% (if the other ends are joined too, this closes an empty loop).  What is
% left is drawn canonically: in every connector the cups (innermost first),
% the straight strands, and the caps (outermost first).
